  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ac 507.01 Advertising and Other Forms of Solicitation. A licensee in public practice shall not seek to obtain clients by advertising or other forms of solicitation in a manner that is false, misleading, or deceptive. Solicitation by the use of coercion, over-reaching, or harassing conduct shall be prohibited.\n\nSource. #1663, eff 12-17-80; ss by #2475, eff 9-13-83; ss by #3061, eff 7-18-85, EXPIRED: 7-18-91\n\nNew. #5366, eff 3-27-92; ss by #6721, INTERIM, eff 3-27-98, EXPIRED: 7-25-98\n\nNew. #6905, eff 12-4-98, EXPIRED: 12-4-06\n\nNew. #8810, INTERIM, eff 1-25-07, EXPIRED: 7-25-07\n\nNew. #9051, eff 12-27-07; ss by #10746, eff 1-1-15; ss by #14188, eff 4-5-25",
